<section class="container py-4 policy-document">
  <h1>Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy</h1>

  <p><strong>Effective Date:</strong>  8 September 2026</p>

  <p>
    Voice of Ex-Servicemen appreciates the support provided by donors through
    our website. This policy explains the terms applicable to cancellation and
    refund requests relating to online donations.
  </p>

  <h2>1. General Policy</h2>

  <p>
    Donations made voluntarily through the Voice of Ex-Servicemen website are
    generally <strong>non-refundable and cannot be cancelled</strong>
    once the donation transaction has been successfully completed.
  </p>

  <p>
    Donors are therefore requested to carefully verify the donation amount and
    payment details before completing the transaction.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Exceptional Refund Requests</h2>

  <p>
    In exceptional circumstances, a donor may contact us regarding a refund
    where the transaction appears to have occurred due to a genuine technical
    error, duplicate payment, or other verifiable issue.
  </p>

  <p>
    Each request will be reviewed individually. A refund, where approved, will
    be subject to verification of the transaction and the applicable procedures
    of the payment gateway, bank, and other payment service providers involved.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Duplicate Transactions</h2>

  <p>
    If a donor believes that the same donation has been charged more than once,
    the donor should contact us as soon as reasonably possible and provide the
    relevant transaction details.
  </p>

  <p>
    After verification, any eligible duplicate payment may be considered for
    refund through the applicable payment channel.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Failed Transactions</h2>

  <p>
    If a payment transaction fails and the donation is not received by Voice of
    Ex-Servicemen, no donation will be considered successfully completed.
  </p>

  <p>
    If the donor's account has nevertheless been debited, the donor should first
    allow reasonable time for the payment system or bank to reconcile the
    transaction. If the amount is not automatically reversed or settled, the
    donor may contact us with the transaction details for verification.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Refund Method</h2>

  <p>
    Where a refund is approved, it will normally be processed through the
    original payment method or through the payment gateway's applicable refund
    mechanism.
  </p>

  <p>
    The time required for the refunded amount to appear in the donor's account
    may depend on the donor's bank, card issuer, UPI service provider, payment
    gateway, or other financial institution.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Information Required for Verification</h2>

  <p>
    To investigate a refund request, we may require information such as the
    donor's name, date of transaction, donation amount, transaction ID, payment
    reference number, and contact details used during the transaction.
  </p>

  <p>
    Donors should never provide their card PIN, CVV, UPI PIN, password, banking
    password, or other confidential payment credentials to us.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Contact for Refund Requests</h2>

  <p>
    Refund-related requests should be submitted through our
    <a href="/contact-us/">Contact Us</a> page with sufficient transaction details
    to allow us to verify the payment.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Changes to This Policy</h2>

  <p>
    Voice of Ex-Servicemen reserves the right to modify this Refund &
    Cancellation Policy from time to time. Any updated version will be published
    on this page with the revised effective date.
  </p>
</section>
